timeline
    title History of Programming Languages
    1801 : Jacquard Loom - Punch cards (first programming)
    1936 : Turing Machine - Theoretical foundation
    1945 : ENIAC - First electronic computer
    1957 : FORTRAN - First high-level language
    1969 : Unix - First OS written in C
    1972 : C Language - Created by Dennis Ritchie at Bell Labs
    1978 : K&R C - The C Programming Language published
    1989 : C89 - First ANSI C standard
    1991 : Python - Created as a beginner language
    1999 : C99 - Major C update (// comments, inline functions)
    2011 : C11 - Multi-threading support added
    2020+ : C is still top 10 - Used in OS, embedded, systems
